WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.382
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 2: Exploring Space.

2
00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:10.505
Unit 2 pairs two information texts about astronomy and
life on the space station with The Burrow Discovery,

3
00:00:10.585 --> 00:00:12.902
a story about a school science fair.

4
00:00:12.982 --> 00:00:18.827
You will study twenty-five words such as
burrow, boycott, glare, cooperate and ownership,

5
00:00:18.907 --> 00:00:24.285
and you will master indefinite pronouns,
singular agreement and adverbial phrases.

6
00:00:24.365 --> 00:00:32.141
You will separate fact from opinion, compare biography with
autobiography, and write a friendly blog post of your own.

7
00:00:32.221 --> 00:00:37.733
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:37.813 --> 00:00:44.570
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
use the twenty-five Unit 2 words about science,

9
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.954
systems and social values accurately in speech and writing.

10
00:00:49.034 --> 00:00:56.980
You will also identify indefinite pronouns in a text
and use them with the matching singular or plural verb.

11
00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:04.486
You will also read an information text about astronomy
and extract main points supported by evidence.

12
00:01:04.566 --> 00:01:07.235
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:07.315 --> 00:01:13.424
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
independence, issue, empire, expose, glare, source.

14
00:01:13.504 --> 00:01:18.591
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:18.671 --> 00:01:22.610
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:27.985
The reading sequence includes The Night
Sky Above Us and Life on the Space Station.

17
00:01:28.065 --> 00:01:28.892
Read actively.

18
00:01:28.972 --> 00:01:33.360
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:37.569
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:37.649 --> 00:01:43.872
The first language focus is Indefinite pronouns:
talking about people and things in general.

21
00:01:43.952 --> 00:01:50.106
Indefinite pronouns stand in for people or
things when we do not need to name them exactly.

22
00:01:50.186 --> 00:01:55.449
One short word can replace a whole list,
which keeps writing smooth and clear.

23
00:01:55.529 --> 00:02:02.916
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:02:02.996 --> 00:02:07.516
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: Astronaut interview role-play.

25
00:02:07.596 --> 00:02:11.738
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:11.818 --> 00:02:14.951
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:15.031 --> 00:02:18.291
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.946
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:20.026 --> 00:02:27.068
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:27.148 --> 00:02:30.522
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:30.602 --> 00:02:38.652
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
